# Line-ending policy for kzen-auto.
#
# The repo previously had core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, while the
# working tree was a mix of LF and CRLF. Any tool that rewrote a file (e.g. a
# bulk `sed -i`) would trip git's autocrlf round-trip check and flag the file as
# modified with a phantom LF<->CRLF change, even when content was unchanged.
#
# Pinning LF everywhere (the natural choice for a cross-platform JVM/Gradle/JS
# project) removes that ambiguity: git stores LF and checks out LF regardless of
# the contributor's core.autocrlf setting.

# Auto-detect text vs binary; store and check out text as LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts must keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never apply EOL normalization (text=auto usually detects these,
# but be explicit so screenshots/jars/fonts can never be corrupted).
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.jar  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
